\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The integral alternating Hurwitz form}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{On the rational Hamilton quaternion algebra, use the
norm pairing
#{\langle x,y\rangle_0=\operatorname{Re}(\bar x y)}.
The \newvocab{integral alternating Hurwitz form} is its
right-multiplication modification restricted to the
Hurwitz lattice #{\mathcal O} of \ref{fdip-00V1}:
##{b_{\mathbb Z}(x,y)=\langle x,y(\qi +\qj)\rangle_0,
 \qquad x,y\in\mathcal O.}
This restriction takes values in #{\mathbb Z}, as proved
in \ref{fdip-00V4}. For a commutative ring #{k}, put
#{F_k=\mathcal O\otimes_{\mathbb Z}k} and define
#{b_k} by scalar extension of #{b_{\mathbb Z}}.
The group #{G=\mathcal O^\times=2T} acts by left
multiplication. Perfectness and invariance of #{b_k} are
proved there as well.}
